cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use EquaSolve in academic work, please cite the published paper below."
title: "EquaSolve: A Zero-Installation Browser-Based Engineering Equation Solver with Embedded Thermophysical Properties, Optimization, and Interactive Visualization"
abstract: >-
  A self-contained HTML/JavaScript application that solves systems of nonlinear
  algebraic equations, ordinary differential equations, parametric sweeps,
  optimization problems, regression fits, and sensitivity and uncertainty
  analyses, with built-in thermophysical property libraries for 38 working
  fluids. Runs offline in any modern browser with no installation.
